  "input_and_result_semantics": [
    "The existing OCEL conformance route gains an opt-in exact OTG relation-threshold map. The native CLI exposes matching inline and file controls. Existing compare_otg algorithms and default workflow are unchanged.",
    "The exact map is an array of NativeString and double-or-IEEE-tag pairs. Omission and explicit empty maps remain distinct transport states. Exact duplicate decoded byte keys, invalid values and conflicts with the five named legacy aliases are rejected by presence.",
    "The existing HTTP library deduplicates byte-identical raw query pairs before exposing parameters. That compatible normalization remains unchanged; distinct query values and query/multipart conflicts are rejected.",
    "Relation names are never trimmed, split or restricted to predefined names. Empty, whitespace, Unicode, embedded NUL, arbitrary bytes and WTF8 are preserved. Native map order is lexical byte order rather than submitted insertion order.",
    "Thresholds support negative finite values, signed zero, finite extremes, subnormals, NaN and signed infinities. IEEE tags preserve comparison semantics rather than arbitrary NaN payload bits.",
    "Matching map entries override the scalar fallback by exact byte key. Native comparison uses a strict greater-than predicate; custom threshold equality suppresses the corresponding deviation.",
    "Real and normative graph or OCEL inputs remain independent. Canonical graph snapshots preserve original vector order, duplicate entries, exact frequencies and labels separately from native comparison normalization.",
    "Complete native deviation results use byte-safe identifiers and nonfinite scalar tags. Original serializer bytes and their transport or presentation errors remain separate from authoritative native data.",
    "Both existing public helpers accept the same exact map and retain original File identities, source hashes, raw responses and reports. The execution workspace also retains complete tables/CSV and direct legacy-byte downloads within its existing navigation and default controls.",
    "Direct native witnesses and API, CLI and client captures establish the implemented workflow. They do not establish full external reference behavior, browser, performance or concurrency parity."
  ],
